#: source/development/documentation.md:1
msgid "Contributing documentation"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:3
msgid ""
"Improvements to documentation are very much appreciated, and a good way to "
"start out with contributing to Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:5
msgid "This is how you can help:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:6
msgid ""
"Address [open issues with documentation](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues?"
"q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3Adocumentation)"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:7
msgid ""
"Review [pull requests concerning documentation](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pulls?q=is%3Apr+is%3Aopen+label%3Adocumentation)"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:9
msgid ""
"Incremental refactorings of the documentation build setup to make it faster "
"or easier to understand and maintain are also welcome."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:11
msgid "Building the manual"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:13
msgid "Build the manual from scratch:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:19
msgid "or"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:25
msgid "and open `./result/share/doc/nix/manual/index.html`."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:28
msgid ""
"To build the manual incrementally, [enter the development shell](./building."
"md) and configure with `doc-gen` enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:30
msgid "**If using interactive `nix develop`:**"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:32
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix develop\n"
"$ mesonFlags=\"$mesonFlags -Ddoc-gen=true\" mesonConfigurePhase\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:37
msgid "**If using direnv:**"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:39
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ direnv allow\n"
"$ bash -c 'source $stdenv/setup && mesonFlags=\"$mesonFlags -Ddoc-gen=true\" "
"mesonConfigurePhase'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:44
msgid "Then build the manual:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:51
msgid ""
"The HTML manual will be generated at `build/src/nix-manual/manual/index."
"html`."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:53
msgid "Style guide"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:55
msgid "The goal of this style guide is to make it such that"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:56
msgid "The manual is easy to search and skim for relevant information"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:57
msgid "Documentation sources are easy to edit"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:58
msgid "Changes to documentation are easy to review"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:60
msgid ""
"You will notice that this is not implemented consistently yet. Please follow "
"the guide when making additions or changes to existing documentation. Do not "
"make sweeping changes, unless they are programmatic and can be validated "
"easily."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:64
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:66
msgid ""
"This manual is [reference documentation](https://diataxis.fr/reference/). "
"The typical usage pattern is to look up isolated pieces of information. It "
"should therefore aim to be correct, consistent, complete, and easy to "
"navigate at a glance."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:70
msgid "Aim for clarity and brevity."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:72
msgid ""
"Please take the time to read the [plain language guidelines](https://www."
"plainlanguage.gov/guidelines/) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:74
msgid "Describe the subject factually."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:76
msgid ""
"In particular, do not make value judgements or recommendations. Check the "
"code or add tests if in doubt."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:79
msgid "Provide complete, minimal examples, and explain them."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:81
msgid ""
"Readers should be able to try examples verbatim and get the same results as "
"shown in the manual. Always describe in words what a given example does."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:84
msgid ""
"Non-trivial examples may need additional explanation, especially if they use "
"concepts from outside the given context."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:86
msgid "Always explain code examples in the text."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:88
msgid ""
"Use comments in code samples very sparingly, for instance to highlight a "
"particular aspect. Readers tend to glance over large amounts of code when "
"scanning for information."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:91
msgid ""
"Especially beginners will likely find reading more complex-looking code "
"strenuous and may therefore avoid it altogether."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:93
msgid ""
"If a code sample appears to require a lot of inline explanation, consider "
"replacing it with a simpler one. If that's not possible, break the example "
"down into multiple parts, explain them separately, and then show the "
"combined result at the end. This should be a last resort, as that would "
"amount to writing a [tutorial](https://diataxis.fr/tutorials/) on the given "
"subject."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:97
msgid "Use British English."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:99
msgid ""
"This is a somewhat arbitrary choice to force consistency, and accounts for "
"the fact that a majority of Nix users and developers are from Europe."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:101
msgid "Links and anchors"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:103
msgid ""
"Reference documentation must be readable in arbitrary order. Readers cannot "
"be expected to have any particular prerequisite knowledge about Nix. While "
"the table of contents can provide guidance and full-text search can help, "
"they are most likely to find what they need by following sensible cross-"
"references."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:107
msgid "Link to technical terms"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:109
msgid ""
"When mentioning Nix-specific concepts, commands, options, settings, etc., "
"link to appropriate documentation. Also link to external tools or concepts, "
"especially if their meaning may be ambiguous. You may also want to link to "
"definitions of less common technical terms."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:113
msgid ""
"Then readers won't have to actively search for definitions and are more "
"likely to discover relevant information on their own."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:115
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:117
msgid ""
"`man` and `--help` pages don't display links. Use appropriate link texts "
"such that readers of terminal output can infer search terms."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:120
msgid "Do not break existing URLs between releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:122
msgid ""
"There are countless links in the wild pointing to old versions of the "
"manual. We want people to find up-to-date documentation when following "
"popular advice."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:125
msgid ""
"When moving files, update [redirects on nixos.org](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nixos-homepage/blob/master/netlify.toml)."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:127
msgid ""
"This is especially important when moving information out of the Nix manual "
"to other resources."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:129
msgid ""
"When changing anchors, update [client-side redirects](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/blob/master/doc/manual/redirects.js)"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:131
msgid ""
"The current setup is cumbersome, and help making better automation is "
"appreciated."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:133
msgid ""
"The build checks for broken internal links with. This happens late in the "
"process, so [building the whole manual](#building-the-manual) is not "
"suitable for iterating quickly. [`mdbook-linkcheck`](https://github.com/"
"Michael-F-Bryan/mdbook-linkcheck) does not implement checking [URI fragments]"
"(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/URI_fragment) yet."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:140
msgid "Markdown conventions"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:142
msgid ""
"The manual is written in markdown, and rendered with [mdBook](https://github."
"com/rust-lang/mdBook) for the web and with [lowdown](https://github.com/"
"kristapsdz/lowdown) for `man` pages and `--help` output."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:144
msgid "For supported markdown features, refer to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:145
msgid ""
"[mdBook documentation](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/format/markdown."
"html)"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:146
msgid "[lowdown documentation](https://kristaps.bsd.lv/lowdown/)"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:148
msgid "Please observe these guidelines to ease reviews:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:150
msgid "Write one sentence per line."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:152
msgid ""
"This makes long sentences immediately visible, and makes it easier to review "
"changes and make direct suggestions."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:154
msgid ""
"Use reference links – sparingly – to ease source readability. Put "
"definitions close to their first use."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:157
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:167
msgid "Use admonitions of the following form:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:175
msgid "Highlight examples as such:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:185
msgid ""
"Highlight syntax definitions as such, using [EBNF](https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/Extended_Backus%E2%80%93Naur_form) notation:"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:193
msgid "The `..` variable"
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:195
msgid ""
"`..` provides a base path for links that occur in reusable snippets or other "
"documentation that doesn't have a base path of its own."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:197
msgid ""
"If a broken link occurs in a snippet that was inserted into multiple "
"generated files in different directories, use `..` to reference the `doc/"
"manual/source` directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/development/documentation.md:199
msgid ""
"If the `..` literal appears in an error message from the [`mdbook-linkcheck`]"
"(https://github.com/Michael-F-Bryan/mdbook-linkcheck) tool, the `..` "
"replacement needs to be applied to the generated source file that mentions "
"it. See existing `..` logic in the \\[Makefile for the manual\\]. Regular "
"markdown files used for the manual have a base path of their own and they "
"can use relative paths instead of `..`."
msgstr ""

